course: dictionary
lesson: 11208
title: Meet the wombat
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A wombat is a sturdy, short-legged animal from Australia. It has a broad head and thick fur, and it digs burrows, which are its underground homes. «Wombats are the only animals known to make cube-shaped droppings» tells you something surprising about them.
explain: Use the words around a new word to find its meaning. «Most Australian mammals are marsupials, whose tiny babies finish growing in a pouch.» The sentence says the babies grow in a pouch, so a marsupial is an animal whose babies grow in a pouch. Check your meaning in a dictionary to be sure.
explain: A wombat's pouch opens backwards. When the mother digs, no soil gets into the pouch and onto her baby. Wombats are nocturnal, which means they are mostly active at night.
fact: A wombat is a short-legged Australian animal with thick fur.
fact: «Marsupial» means an animal whose babies grow in a pouch.
fact: Wombats dig burrows and eat grass and roots.
fact: Wombats make cube-shaped droppings, which do not roll off rocks and logs, so they can mark their area.
fact: «Diprotodon» was a giant pouched relative of wombats that lived in Australia until about 40,000 years ago.
exercise: What is a wombat? | A tall bird that lives in Africa | A small insect that flies at night | *A sturdy, short-legged Australian marsupial
exercise: «Wombats are the only animals known to make cube-shaped droppings, which do not roll away.» Why does this help a wombat? | The droppings float, so they are easy to find | The droppings are hidden inside burrows | *The droppings stay in place, so they can mark its area | The droppings are soft and sticky
exercise: «Most Australian mammals are marsupials, whose tiny babies finish growing in a pouch.» Find and copy the word that means an animal whose babies grow in a pouch. | pouch | mammals | *marsupials | babies
test: In which country do wombats live? | Canada | Brazil | South Africa | *Australia
test: What prize did the scientists who found out about cube-shaped droppings win? | *An Ig Nobel Prize in 2019 | A gold medal at the Olympics | A prize for reading aloud | A prize for the biggest animal
exam: Why is a wombat's backward-opening pouch useful when it digs? | It helps the wombat swim faster | It makes the wombat easier to see at night | It stores food for the winter | *It keeps soil out, so the baby stays clean
